join Zanele (Neutral) left
join Hope (Neutral) right
update Zanele (Worried)
join Mama Zulu (Neutral) left
Mama Zulu: Eat that tonight. Not tomorrow — tonight.
Zanele: Mama, you cannot keep —
Mama Zulu: I can.
Zanele: At least let me —
Mama Zulu: No.
- Does she do that often?
	Hope: Does she do that often?
	Zanele: Every few weeks, for about six years, and she has never once let me pay her or thank her properly.
	Zanele: I have decided that the thanking is not the part she wants. So I eat it, and I make sure she can see the empty pot when I return it.
	Zanele: That seems to be the arrangement. It took me a while to work out what the arrangement was.
